# Site configuration for the shared OpenNebula devcontainer layer.
#
# Copy to .devcontainer/site.env and edit. This file holds everything that
# legitimately differs between projects; common/setup.sh sources it with `set -a`
# so every value is exported.
#
# This file is COMMITTED and must contain no secrets. Credentials live in
# ~/.one/one_auth_<SUFFIX> on the host and are never copied into the repo.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment selection (required)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Picks which credential pair to load from the read-only ~/.one bind mount:
#   ~/.one/one_auth_<SUFFIX>   credentials, user:password
#   ~/.one/one_url_<SUFFIX>    shell assignments for ONE_URL, ONE_XMLRPC, ONEFLOW_URL
#
# Hardcoding this per repo makes credential selection deterministic. Projects on
# this campus authenticate against the SAME shared OpenNebula instance, so a
# mis-selection silently operates as the wrong user rather than failing loudly -
# which is exactly why there is no interactive picker by default.
OPENNEBULA_DEPLOYMENT_ENVIRONMENT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interactive credential picker (optional, default off)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to be prompted to choose from all one_auth_* files at container
# create instead of using the suffix above. Only enable where operating as the
# wrong user is an inconvenience rather than a hazard.
# ONE_ALLOW_INTERACTIVE_SELECT=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version pinning
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two distinct mechanisms, easy to confuse:
#
#   *_VERSION_OVERRIDE   always wins, whether or not detection would have worked.
#                        Use to force a specific version.
#   *_VERSION_FALLBACK   applies ONLY when live detection against the server
#                        fails (no VPN, server down, no credentials yet).
#
# The CLI gem and the PyONE Python bindings are pinned independently because
# they do not necessarily agree on which release works against a given server.
# Setup fails loudly if detection fails and no fallback is set - better than
# silently installing a mismatched version.
OPENNEBULA_CLI_VERSION_FALLBACK="~> 7.4"
PYONE_VERSION_FALLBACK="~=7.4.0"

# Force a specific version regardless of what the server reports:
# OPENNEBULA_CLI_VERSION_OVERRIDE="~> 7.4"
# PYONE_VERSION_OVERRIDE="~=7.4.0"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SSH host aliases (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Space-separated alias:hostname:keyfile triples, written to ~/.ssh/config at
# setup if absent. The ~/.ssh directory is bind-mounted from the host so the key
# files are always present, but the host's config may not define these aliases
# on a fresh machine - writing them here means git remotes work after a rebuild
# with no manual host configuration.
#
# IdentitiesOnly yes is always set, so SSH does not offer other loaded agent
# keys first and get rejected by a server that only accepts the matching one.
# SSH_ALIASES="git-example:git.example.ac.uk:~/.ssh/id_ed25519"
